WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.740 --> 00:00:05.870
I told you about six weeks ago that the Trump
administration's then new strategy on the

00:00:05.870 --> 00:00:09.290
virus would be to pretend the virus has been
fixed.

00:00:09.290 --> 00:00:10.540
We are past the peak.

00:00:10.540 --> 00:00:14.410
They were saying they're not going to do any
more press briefings with doctors.

00:00:14.410 --> 00:00:17.050
Very little talking about the virus or treatments
or vaccines.

00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:21.420
They'll instead focus on reopening the economy,
restaurants, recovery, all of that stuff.

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:22.859
And that's exactly what happened.

00:00:22.859 --> 00:00:27.949
And meanwhile, as I already told you earlier,
cases have exploded in places like Florida,

00:00:27.949 --> 00:00:32.080
which is hitting higher and higher new highs
in terms of cases every day.

00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:36.370
Places like Texas, whose curve is slightly
less horrifying than Florida's, but still

00:00:36.370 --> 00:00:37.510
really bad.

00:00:37.510 --> 00:00:38.940
So what does Donald Trump do?

00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:44.070
He decides he'll have a huge rally in Tulsa,
Oklahoma, because that's how you pretend things

00:00:44.070 --> 00:00:47.130
are totally normal, except things aren't totally
normal.

00:00:47.130 --> 00:00:52.340
And they know it because when you go to register
for tickets, you have to accept a waiver that

00:00:52.340 --> 00:00:57.720
says if you catch coronavirus at the rally,
you will not hold Trump's campaign or the

00:00:57.720 --> 00:00:59.850
event organizers responsible.

00:00:59.850 --> 00:01:05.390
The exact wording is that by clicking register
below, you acknowledge that an inherent risk

00:01:05.390 --> 00:01:09.900
of exposure to covert 19 exists in any public
space where people are present.

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:14.920
By attending the rally, you and any guests
voluntarily assume all risks related to exposure

00:01:14.920 --> 00:01:19.149
to Kova 19 and agree not to hold Donald Trump
for president.

00:01:19.149 --> 00:01:24.679
The be the Bok Center or anybody else liable
for illness or injury.

00:01:24.679 --> 00:01:28.979
That sure doesn't sound like things are normal,
and that certainly doesn't sound like it's

00:01:28.979 --> 00:01:31.460
the type of situation where you should be
having a huge rally.

00:01:31.460 --> 00:01:34.799
Now, of course, Trump is protecting himself.

00:01:34.799 --> 00:01:37.159
Trump's protecting his campaign.

00:01:37.159 --> 00:01:39.399
But will he be protecting the people who are
there?

00:01:39.399 --> 00:01:44.539
Will they hand out masks to everybody on the
way in and say where the mask during the rally?

00:01:44.539 --> 00:01:48.579
Will they space people out so that they can
maintain some physical distance?

00:01:48.579 --> 00:01:50.000
No, they appear.

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:53.719
The answer appears to be they're not going
to do any of those things when a rally needs

00:01:53.719 --> 00:01:55.679
a medical warning label.

00:01:55.679 --> 00:01:57.420
Maybe the rally shouldn't be happening.

00:01:57.420 --> 00:02:02.310
Now, there's some very interesting sociology
and social psychology here.

00:02:02.310 --> 00:02:04.380
We've talked about Trump ism as a cult.

00:02:04.380 --> 00:02:05.790
And we've interviewed cult experts.

00:02:05.790 --> 00:02:07.679
And this is sort of a test.

00:02:07.679 --> 00:02:13.700
When Jim Jones had his cult down in Guyana,
he did a test run of having them drink cyanide

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:16.950
laced Kool-Aid where he didn't really put
the cyanide in the Kool-Aid.

00:02:16.950 --> 00:02:20.890
This is where the term to drink the Kool-Aid
originated.

00:02:20.890 --> 00:02:25.630
And the reason Jim Jones did this was to see
how devoted his cult followers were.

00:02:25.630 --> 00:02:30.960
And then later on, he actually gave them the
cyanide laced Kool-Aid and 900 people died.

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:33.010
This is the Trump ism test.

00:02:33.010 --> 00:02:37.570
Are you willing to go despite the waiver,
despite it obviously not being safe to do

00:02:37.570 --> 00:02:42.300
an event this big in this crowded to pledge
your support for the deal?

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:43.300
Dear Leader.

00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:46.560
Now, you might be wondering, what are right
wingers saying about this disclaimer?

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:48.180
I looked around.

00:02:48.180 --> 00:02:53.640
A lot of them are saying, you liberal goons,
every big event is going to have a disclaimer

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:56.010
like this until we have a corona virus vaccine.

00:02:56.010 --> 00:03:00.560
There's nothing special about a Trump rally
having this waiver.

00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:04.870
What's special is that nobody else is having
events with 10000 people right now.

00:03:04.870 --> 00:03:11.230
Other events might have a similar disclaimer
if they start having events this big, if it's

00:03:11.230 --> 00:03:12.840
safe to start.

00:03:12.840 --> 00:03:15.090
But there are no such events going on.

00:03:15.090 --> 00:03:16.090
That's the whole point.

00:03:16.090 --> 00:03:21.550
The fact that such a disclaimer is necessary
when you're the only people having an event

00:03:21.550 --> 00:03:25.810
this big, that's a sign you shouldn't be having
